
%9Syntax:%9

TKLIST %|[<mask>]

%9Parameters:%9

    An optional mask passed to the server as the STATS argument.

%9Description:%9

    Sends STATS k to the server of the active window, asking for the list
    of temporary K-lines (tklines) on ircd 2.11. erssi shows the server's
    reply like any other. A command of the tk.pl script; /TK LIST does the
    same.

    The argument must be a single word (up to 64 characters) - anything
    else is ignored and a plain STATS k is sent. The script does not check
    privileges; the server decides whether to show the list to someone
    without IRC operator status.

%9Examples:%9

    /TKLIST
    /TKLIST *@*.example.org

%9See also:%9 KLIST, STATS, TK, TKL, UNTKL

